{"type":"message","id":"ee9e8792","parentId":"f5b7013a","timestamp":"2026-05-19T05:12:29.732Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Lucus also doesn't have permission. Let me try Codus.\n\nActually, I think the issue here is that none of the bots have the wiki:wiki permission. This is a permission issue on the Feishu app side, not an API calling issue.\n\nLet me be honest with the user about this situation. The apps don't have the required permissions to access the wiki. The user needs to grant wiki:wiki permission to one of the Feishu apps in the Feishu Open Platform.\n\nActually wait - let me also try the xiaoye account before giving up, just in case.\n\nActually, the error message says \"tenant needs read permission\" which suggests that maybe a different permission scope is needed, or maybe I need to use user token instead of tenant token, or there's some other issue.\n\nActually, let me try using the docx API directly since maybe I can extract the document token from the wiki URL in a different way. The wiki link structure might have a document ID embedded in it that I can use.\n\nActually wait - let me check if maybe there's a different API I should be calling. The wiki node token gives me the space_id and obj_token when I call the right API. But the issue is permissions.\n\nLet me tell the user about the permission issue and ask them to grant the wiki:wiki permission to the Talus app.\n\nActually wait - the user sent me this wiki link and asked me to test editing it. They presumably have access to it. Maybe I should try to get the document content using a different method - perhaps by using the feishu doc API with a document token if I can find one.\n\nActually, I just realized - maybe I can search for the document using the Feishu search API, or maybe there's a way to get the obj_token from the wiki token using a different endpoint.\n\nLet me try one more thing - the Feishu wiki API might have a different endpoint for getting node info. Let me check the documentation for the correct endpoint.\n\nActually, looking at the error more carefully - it says \"tenant needs read permission\". This suggests that the tenant (the app) doesn't have permission, not the user. So the app needs to be granted wiki:wiki permission in the Feishu Open Platform.\n\nLet me just tell the user what the issue is and ask them to grant the permission.\n\nActually, wait - let me try one more thing. The wiki link is `https://yio5us4oqe.feishu.cn/wiki/MKJtwW9nriMKh3kMmz4c3Bubnoc`. \n\nLet me also check if this is a cloud wiki or a legacy wiki - they might use different APIs. Let me also try checking the document directly using the doc API - maybe the wiki token can be converted to a doc token somehow.\n\nActually I think the most straightforward thing is to ask the user to grant wiki:wiki permission to the Talus app. That's the actual fix needed here.\n\nLet me explain this to the user","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":".\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"App 权限不足，无法访问 Wiki 节点。几个测试的 Bot 账号都没有 `wiki:wiki` 权限。\n\n**问题：** Feishu App (cli_aa8198b425389cef / Talus) 未开通 Wiki 权限。\n\n**解决方案：** 需要在 [Feishu Open Platform](https://open.feishu.cn/app/cli_aa8198b425389cef/auth) 给 Talus App 开通 `wiki:wiki` 或 `wiki:wiki:readonly` 权限。\n\n开通后告诉我，我再重新测试。\n\n---\n\n如果你只是想验证文档编辑功能，我也可以用另一个有文档权限的账号测试一个你自己创建的测试文档。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":26708,"output":752,"cacheRead":80,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27540,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779167522037,"responseId":"chatcmpl-3bee5619-a1e6-4ade-ae6c-b7385a505b01"}}
