{"type":"message","id":"aa4b877a","parentId":"3ccaa71d","timestamp":"2026-05-19T08:36:54.868Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Boss is asking about MCP (Model Context Protocol) vs adding wiki permissions. Let me think about this.\n\nOpenClaw has a Feishu extension that provides `feishu_wiki` and `feishu_doc` tools. These are built-in tools that make API calls directly using the bot's credentials.\n\nMCP (Model Context Protocol) is a different way to expose tools - it's a protocol that allows AI models to connect to external tools/servers. OpenClaw may support MCP servers as well.\n\nThe question seems to be about whether to:\n1. Add wiki permissions to the existing Feishu bot app (so the built-in `feishu_wiki` tool works)\n2. Use MCP to connect to Feishu\n\nFor OpenClaw's built-in Feishu integration, you just need to add the permissions to the Feishu app and the tools will work. MCP is a different integration path.\n\nLet me check if OpenClaw supports MCP for Feishu or if there's an MCP server option.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n这是两个不同路径：\n\n**OpenClaw 内置的 Feishu 工具（推荐）：**\n- 直接用 Bot 的权限，配置简单\n- 需要给 Feishu App 开通 `wiki:wiki` 权限\n- 工具已经内置，直接用 `feishu_wiki` / `feishu_doc` 调用\n\n**MCP（Model Context Protocol）：**\n- 另一种工具暴露方式\n- 如果 OpenClaw 有 Feishu MCP Server 也可以用\n- 但配置更复杂，一般不推荐\n\n---\n\n**直接回答你的问题：**\n\n加 `wiki:wiki` 权限就行，这是最简单的方式。MCP 不是必须的，OpenClaw 内置的 Feishu 工具已经够用了。\n\n你现在去开通权限，我马上继续测试。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":23842,"output":374,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24328,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779179748648,"responseId":"chatcmpl-3d5ade28-c101-4096-b29d-c82e55d5b7b4"}}
