{"type":"message","id":"d0127f3b","parentId":"97d1b90c","timestamp":"2026-05-19T09:08:05.397Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There seems to be an issue with the API format. Let me check the Feishu docx API documentation format more carefully. The issue might be that `page_size` in the query parameter is `page_size` not `pageSize`. Let me also check if the blocks API has a different format requirement. The error is \"invalid param\", which means the JSON format might be wrong.\n\nActually, I just realized I'm using the wrong API. The children API for docx blocks uses `page_token` not `document_revision_id`. Let me try without that parameter.\n\nActually, looking at the Feishu API docs, the block children API might need `document_revision_id` as a query param, not in the body. Let me try:\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the result - the block_type is 1 which is \"page\". And the block_id is `GX6PdAPdworxHlx4BFecp7FinZe`.\n \nLet me test the blocks API directly to see what response I get and understand the actual format requirements better.\n\nActually, the API error \"invalid param\" could mean the auth token is fine but the request body format is wrong. I'm wondering if `text_element_style` with all those false values is the culprit, or if there's a type issue with the block_type numbers. The Feishu API uses different numbers for block types than what I might be assuming - text is 12, heading1 is 2, etc. Let me try a minimal request first to isolate whether it's a auth issue or a format issue.\n\nLooking at the error code 1770001 which indicates parameter validation failure, I think the problem is that I'm sending `style: {}` as an object when the API expects `style: null` for unset styles. Let me start with just a text block and no style field to simplify things.\n\nActually, I should just attempt a basic write to the doc using the write action and see if the feishu_doc tool can handle it, since the user is asking about OpenClaw's capabilities anyway. But first I need to figure out why the children API call is failing - let me check what scope the token actually has, since I can create documents but might be missing the `docx:document` scope needed for writing blocks.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-6d9e0e76-e400-4d04-8dc9-7b0378ef1a81","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/GX6PdAPdworxHlx4BFecp7FinZe/blocks/GX6PdAPdworxHlx4BFecp7FinZe/children\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer t-g1045jh3ZRYUR2NDO3AFUWD4PQ3O3H4AGLIKWTF3\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"children\": [\n      {\n        \"block_type\": 12,\n        \"text\": {\n          \"elements\": [{\"text_run\": {\"content\": \"测试内容\"}}]\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }'","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":904,"output":663,"cacheRead":25632,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27199,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779181635910,"responseId":"chatcmpl-e620e44f-e312-4160-b8e8-40e175298e7c"}}
