{"type":"message","id":"a8165e67","parentId":"74e1a1e5","timestamp":"2026-05-19T09:12:35.333Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-a906ca4b-5e98-4624-b312-7c9ea1170c47","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"async function insertBlocksWithDescendant(client, docToken, blocks, firstLevelBlockIds, { parentBlockId = docToken, index = -1 } = {}) {\n\tconst descendants = cleanBlocksForDescendant(blocks);\n\tif (descendants.length === 0) return { children: [] };\n\tconst res = await client.docx.documentBlockDescendant.create({\n\t\tpath: {\n\t\t\tdocument_id: docToken,\n\t\t\tblock_id: parentBlockId\n\t\t},\n\t\tdata: {\n\t\t\tchildren_id: firstLevelBlockIds,\n\t\t\tdescendants: descendants.map(toDescendantBlock),\n\t\t\tindex\n\t\t}\n\t});\n\tif (res.code !== 0) throw new Error(`${res.msg} (code: ${res.code})`);\n\treturn { children: res.data?.children ?? [] };\n}\nasync function clearDocumentContent(client, docToken) {\n\tconst existing = await client.docx.documentBlock.list({ path: { document_id: docToken } });\n\tif (existing.code !== 0) throw new Error(existing.msg);\n\tconst childIds = existing.data?.items?.filter((b) => b.parent_id === docToken && b.block_type !== 1).map((b) => b.block_id) ?? [];\n\tif (childIds.length > 0) {\n\t\tconst res = await client.docx.documentBlockChildren.batchDelete({\n\t\t\tpath: {\n\t\t\t\tdocument_id: docToken,\n\t\t\t\tblock_id: docToken\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t\tdata: {\n\t\t\t\tstart_index: 0,\n\t\t\t\tend_index: childIds.length\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t});\n\t\tif (res.code !== 0) throw new Error(res.msg);\n\t}\n\treturn childIds.length;\n}\nasync function uploadImageToDocx(client, blockId, imageBuffer, fileName, docToken) {\n\tconst fileToken = (await client.drive.media.uploadAll({ data: {\n\t\tfile_name: fileName,\n\t\tparent_type: \"docx_image\",\n\t\tparent_node: blockId,\n\t\tsize: imageBuffer.length,\n\t\tfile: imageBuffer,\n\t\t...docToken ? { extra: JSON.stringify({ drive_route_token: docToken }) } : {}\n\t} }))?.file_token;\n\tif (!fileToken) throw new Error(\"Image upload failed: no file_token returned\");\n\treturn fileToken;\n}\nasync function downloadImage(url, maxBytes) {\n\treturn (await getFeishuRuntime().channel.media.fetchRemoteMedia({\n\t\turl,\n\t\tmaxBytes\n\t})).buffer;\n}\nasync function resolveUploadInput(url, filePath, maxBytes, localRoots, explicitFileName, imageInput) {\n\tconst inputSources = [\n\t\turl ? \"url\" : null,\n\t\tfilePath ? \"file_path\" : null,\n\t\timageInput ? \"image\" : null\n\t].filter(Boolean);\n\tif (inputSources.length > 1) throw new Error(`Provide only one image source; got: ${inputSources.join(\", \")}`);\n\tif (imageInput?.startsWith(\"data:\")) {\n\t\tconst commaIdx = imageInput.indexOf(\",\");\n\t\tif (commaIdx === -1) throw new Error(\"Invalid data URI: missing comma separator.\");\n\t\tconst header = imageInput.slice(0, commaIdx);\n\t\tconst data = imageInput.slice(commaIdx + 1);\n\t\tif (!header.includes(\";base64\")) throw new Error(\"Invalid data URI: missing ';base64' marker. Expected format: data:image/png;base64,<base64data>\");"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":17,"aggregated":"async function insertBlocksWithDescendant(client, docToken, blocks, firstLevelBlockIds, { parentBlockId = docToken, index = -1 } = {}) {\n\tconst descendants = cleanBlocksForDescendant(blocks);\n\tif (descendants.length === 0) return { children: [] };\n\tconst res = await client.docx.documentBlockDescendant.create({\n\t\tpath: {\n\t\t\tdocument_id: docToken,\n\t\t\tblock_id: parentBlockId\n\t\t},\n\t\tdata: {\n\t\t\tchildren_id: firstLevelBlockIds,\n\t\t\tdescendants: descendants.map(toDescendantBlock),\n\t\t\tindex\n\t\t}\n\t});\n\tif (res.code !== 0) throw new Error(`${res.msg} (code: ${res.code})`);\n\treturn { children: res.data?.children ?? [] };\n}\nasync function clearDocumentContent(client, docToken) {\n\tconst existing = await client.docx.documentBlock.list({ path: { document_id: docToken } });\n\tif (existing.code !== 0) throw new Error(existing.msg);\n\tconst childIds = existing.data?.items?.filter((b) => b.parent_id === docToken && b.block_type !== 1).map((b) => b.block_id) ?? [];\n\tif (childIds.length > 0) {\n\t\tconst res = await client.docx.documentBlockChildren.batchDelete({\n\t\t\tpath: {\n\t\t\t\tdocument_id: docToken,\n\t\t\t\tblock_id: docToken\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t\tdata: {\n\t\t\t\tstart_index: 0,\n\t\t\t\tend_index: childIds.length\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t});\n\t\tif (res.code !== 0) throw new Error(res.msg);\n\t}\n\treturn childIds.length;\n}\nasync function uploadImageToDocx(client, blockId, imageBuffer, fileName, docToken) {\n\tconst fileToken = (await client.drive.media.uploadAll({ data: {\n\t\tfile_name: fileName,\n\t\tparent_type: \"docx_image\",\n\t\tparent_node: blockId,\n\t\tsize: imageBuffer.length,\n\t\tfile: imageBuffer,\n\t\t...docToken ? { extra: JSON.stringify({ drive_route_token: docToken }) } : {}\n\t} }))?.file_token;\n\tif (!fileToken) throw new Error(\"Image upload failed: no file_token returned\");\n\treturn fileToken;\n}\nasync function downloadImage(url, maxBytes) {\n\treturn (await getFeishuRuntime().channel.media.fetchRemoteMedia({\n\t\turl,\n\t\tmaxBytes\n\t})).buffer;\n}\nasync function resolveUploadInput(url, filePath, maxBytes, localRoots, explicitFileName, imageInput) {\n\tconst inputSources = [\n\t\turl ? \"url\" : null,\n\t\tfilePath ? \"file_path\" : null,\n\t\timageInput ? \"image\" : null\n\t].filter(Boolean);\n\tif (inputSources.length > 1) throw new Error(`Provide only one image source; got: ${inputSources.join(\", \")}`);\n\tif (imageInput?.startsWith(\"data:\")) {\n\t\tconst commaIdx = imageInput.indexOf(\",\");\n\t\tif (commaIdx === -1) throw new Error(\"Invalid data URI: missing comma separator.\");\n\t\tconst header = imageInput.slice(0, commaIdx);\n\t\tconst data = imageInput.slice(commaIdx + 1);\n\t\tif (!header.includes(\";base64\")) throw new Error(\"Invalid data URI: missing ';base64' marker. Expected format: data:image/png;base64,<base64data>\");","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779181955333}}
{"type":"message","id":"33843c36","parentId":"a8165e67","timestamp":"2026-05-19T09:13:29.700Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand. The feishu_doc tool uses `documentBlockDescendant.create` which is a different API endpoint than `documentBlockChildren.create`. This is a batch API for inserting blocks with descendants.\n\nThe format is:\n```\nPOST /open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{document_id}/blocks/{block_id}/descendant\n{\n  \"children_id\": [...],\n  \"descendants\": [...],\n  \"index\": -1\n}\n```\n\nThis might be a newer API that allows inserting a tree of blocks in one call. This might explain why my direct API calls were failing - I was using `documentBlockChildren.create` but the feishu_doc tool uses `documentBlockDescendant.create`.\n\nSo the issue was not permissions but the API endpoint I was using. The feishu_doc tool has access to this batch API. But I was trying to use the regular children API.\n\n\nNow I need to verify if my direct calls are actually hitting scope issues or just using the wrong endpoint. The feishu_doc tool works through the SDK which handles the API format correctly, so if I have the right permissions, the write operation should work. Since the create document operation succeeded, it means I at least have `drive:drive` scope. Let me check what scope is needed for `docx:document.block` operations.\n\nThe error code 1770001 points to invalid parameters rather than a permission denied error, which suggests the issue is with the API format rather than lacking `docx:document.block:create` permission. If that were missing, I'd see a 99991672 error instead. So my direct API calls are failing because I'm using the wrong endpoint format - I should be using `documentBlockDescendant.create` instead of `documentBlockChildren.create`.\n\nSince the write operation works through the feishu_doc tool, the real question is whether the user wants to test the actual tool or debug their direct API calls. Let me try testing with the feishu_doc tool directly instead.\n\nActually, I realize I can't invoke the tools myself—the user needs to do that. But based on my tests, I can confirm the bot has `drive:drive` permissions for creating documents, and the feishu_doc tool uses a different API format that should work. Let me just inform the user about what I've found.\n\nThe issue with my direct API calls was that I was using the wrong endpoint—I needed to use `documentBlockDescendant.create` instead of `documentBlockChildren.create`. Since the OpenClaw feishu_doc tool has the correct implementation, it should work fine. I should give the user a clear summary of the permissions status and what the actual problem was. I need to verify if the feishu_doc tool is actually functioning by running a test, or at minimum confirm the user has the `wiki:wiki` permission we identified as missing. Let me try accessing the wiki node directly with a token to see if permission is the real blocker.\n\nIf the wiki endpoint works, then the tool can navigate and read wiki nodes, but if it fails with a permission error, that confirms the scope isn't enabled. I should focus on getting that permission issue resolved first since that's what's currently blocking progress.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n我直接用 Feishu API 排查了一下问题：\n\n**测试结果：**\n- ✅ 创建文档：有权限（刚创建了 `GX6PdAPdworxHlx4BFecp7FinZe`）\n- ❌ 写入内容 blocks API：报错 1770001（参数格式问题）\n- ❌ Wiki 节点访问：报错 99991672（**缺 `wiki:wiki` 权限**）\n\n**根本原因：**\n1. **Wiki 权限缺 `wiki:wiki`** — 这是主要问题，Bot 无法访问 wiki 节点\n2. blocks API 的格式我没调对（Feishu docx API 比较复杂）\n\n**你需要做的：**\n去 Feishu Open Platform 开通 Talus App 的 `wiki:wiki` 权限：\nhttps://open.feishu.cn/app/cli_aa8198b425389cef/auth\n\n开通后我立刻测试。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":801,"output":847,"cacheRead":32832,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34480,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"st