{"type":"message","id":"0f39947a","parentId":"f3c51c95","timestamp":"2026-05-19T09:50:51.502Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The delete endpoint might be different. Let me check what API is used. Looking at the code around line 836, it uses `client.docx.documentBlockChildren.batchDelete`. Let me try the batch delete endpoint.\n\nActually, looking at the Feishu API docs, the batch delete endpoint is:\n`DELETE /open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{document_id}/blocks/{block_id}/children/batch_delete`\n\nWith body: `{ \"start_index\": number, \"end_index\": number }`\n\nBut I got 404. Let me try without the `/batch_delete` suffix:\n\nActually wait, the endpoint pattern for batch delete in the code is `documentBlockChildren.batchDelete` which in the Feishu SDK maps to `DELETE /open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{document_id}/blocks/{block_id}/children/batch_delete`\n\n\nLet me verify that path is correct.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-4d5f50ec-ea15-4bbc-8c06-eaffd73ac8d0","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# 用正确的 batch_delete 端点\ncurl -s -X DELETE \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/DLi8duiTcoqOZIxixlucMSZ6ndef/blocks/DLi8duiTcoqOZIxixlucMSZ6ndef/children/batch_delete\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer t-g1045jh3ZRYUR2NDO3AFUWD4PQ3O3H4AGLIKWTF3\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"start_index\": 0, \"end_index\": 3}'","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":701,"output":362,"cacheRead":37856,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38919,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779184233289,"responseId":"chatcmpl-032284f7-661a-43ca-8bd9-271f22965bc9"}}
