{"type":"message","id":"836a91e2","parentId":"3404734c","timestamp":"2026-05-19T09:51:38.555Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the `insertBlocks` function uses `client.docx.documentBlockChildren.create`. The format is:\n```json\n{\n  \"children\": [block],\n  \"index\": number\n}\n```\n\nThe block format comes from `toCreateChildBlock(block)`:\n```javascript\nfunction toCreateChildBlock(block) {\n    return block;\n}\n```\n\nSo it passes the block directly. Let me now try the correct API endpoint. Looking at the path:\n- `path: { document_id: docToken, block_id: blockId }`\n- `data: { children: [block], index: optional }\n\nSo the HTTP endpoint should be:\n`POST https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{docToken}/blocks/{blockId}/children`\n\n\nwith the request body containing the children array and optional index. I was sending block_type 2 (Text) blocks before, but looking at the Feishu docs, block_type 12 is Bullet while 2 is actually Text. Let me test with a simple text block structure like `{\"children\": [{\"block_type\": 2, \"text\": {\"elements\": [{\"text_run\": {\"content\": \"Hello\"}}]}}]}`.\n\nThe earlier error with code 1770001 might have been due to using the wrong root block ID or missing required fields in the block structure itself.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-fe0436c6-83b2-43af-aed5-ccb157a95ca6","name":"exec","arguments":{"timeout":10,"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/DLi8duiTcoqOZIxixlucMSZ6ndf/blocks/DLi8duiTcoqOZIxixlucMSZ6ndf/children\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer t-g1045jh3ZRYUR2NDO3AFUWD4PQ3O3H4AGLIKWTF3\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"children\": [\n      {\n        \"block_type\": 2,\n        \"text\": {\n          \"elements\": [{\"text_run\": {\"content\": \"Talus测试写入\"}}]\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"index\": 0\n  }'"}